    "lesson": {
      "title": "How tall is the tree?",
      "instruction": "Aim your sight line at the top of the tree. How tall is it? Then step back and aim again.",
      "explanation": "Where the sight line meets the tree is eye height + distance × tan(angle); aimed at the top, that is the tree's height. The angle is limited to 80° because a vertical sight line has no triangle."
    },
